# ☁️ SaaS vs PaaS vs IaaS
🔹 1. Application
👉 Application = jo software user use karta hai

SaaS:
✔ Provider manage karta hai
👉 Tum bas use karte ho (no coding)
👉 Kyon?
→ SaaS ready-made software hota hai, isliye user ko kuch banane ki zarurat nahi

PaaS:
✔ User manage karta hai
👉 Tum apna app develop karte ho
👉 Kyon?
→ Platform diya jata hai app banane ke liye

IaaS:
✔ User manage karta hai
👉 Tum app install + control karte ho
👉 Kyon?
→ Yaha full control hota hai, isliye sab tumhe karna padta hai

🔹 2. Data
👉 Data = user ki files / database

SaaS:
✔ Provider manage karta hai
👉 Tum direct control nahi karte
👉 Kyon?
→ SaaS me pura system company ka hota hai

PaaS:
✔ User manage karta hai
👉 Tum database handle karte ho
👉 Kyon?
→ Tum apna app bana rahe ho, to data bhi tumhara

IaaS:
✔ User manage karta hai
👉 Full control (store, backup, security)
👉 Kyon?
→ Infrastructure mila hai, data bhi tumhe hi manage karna hoga

🔹 3. Runtime
👉 Runtime = jahan code run hota hai (Java, Python etc.)

SaaS:
✔ Provider
👉 Tumhe runtime ki tension nahi
👉 Kyon?
→ Tum sirf app use karte ho

PaaS:
✔ Provider
👉 Ready environment milta hai
👉 Kyon?
→ Focus sirf coding par hota hai

IaaS:
✔ User
👉 Tum khud runtime install karte ho
👉 Kyon?
→ Full control = sab setup tumhe karna padega


🔹 4. Middleware
👉 Middleware = app aur OS ke beech ka software

SaaS:
✔ Provider
👉 Tum use bhi nahi dekhte
👉 Kyon?
→ Everything hidden hota hai

PaaS:
✔ Provider
👉 Automatically manage hota hai
👉 Kyon?
→ Developer ko easy banane ke liye

IaaS:
✔ User
👉 Tum install + manage karte ho
👉 Kyon?
→ Infrastructure mila hai, baaki sab tumhara


🔹 5. Operating System
👉 OS = Windows / Linux

SaaS:
✔ Provider
👉 Tumhe pata bhi nahi hota kaunsa OS hai
👉 Kyon?
→ Fully managed service

PaaS:
✔ Provider
👉 OS ka tension nahi
👉 Kyon?
→ Tum sirf app bana rahe ho

IaaS:
✔ User
👉 Tum OS install + update karte ho
👉 Kyon?
→ Full system control tumhare paas

🔹 6. Virtualization
👉 Virtual machine banane ki technology

SaaS: ✔ Provider
PaaS: ✔ Provider
IaaS: ✔ Provider

👉 Kyon?
→ Ye backend technology hai, user ko direct access nahi diya jata

🔹 7. Servers
👉 Physical machines

SaaS: ✔ Provider
PaaS: ✔ Provider
IaaS: ✔ Provider

👉 Kyon?
→ Real hardware company ke paas hota hai

🔹 8. Storage
👉 Data store karne ki jagah

SaaS: ✔ Provider
PaaS: ✔ Provider
IaaS: ✔ Provider

👉 Kyon?
→ Storage infrastructure cloud company deti hai

🔹 9. Networking
👉 Internet, routing, connectivity

SaaS: ✔ Provider
PaaS: ✔ Provider
IaaS: ✔ Provider

👉 Kyon?
→ Networking setup complex hota hai, isliye provider manage karta hai


