# ☁️ 1. On-Demand Service

On-demand service ek aisa model hai jisme user bina kisi human interaction ke automatically computing resources (server, storage, database) le sakta hai whenever needed.

🎯 Purpose (Kyon use hota hai)
Instant resource availability
Manual process remove karna
Fast development & deployment
Developer productivity increase

⚙️ Setup (Kaise hota hai)
Cloud provider apne data centers me resources ready rakhta hai
User:
-Web console / dashboard
-API / CLI tools
-use karke resource request karta hai
System automatically resource allocate kar deta hai
Example using Amazon Web Services:
-EC2 instance launch → few clicks → server ready

🔥 Use (Real Use Case)
Developer ko testing ke liye server chahiye
Turant create karta hai → kaam complete → delete


# ☁️ 2. Resource Pooling

Resource pooling ek concept hai jisme cloud provider apne computing resources (servers, storage, network) ko ek shared pool me organize karta hai aur multiple users ko serve karta hai (multi-tenant model).

🎯 Purpose (Kyon use hota hai)
Cost efficiency (shared resources)
Better utilization of hardware
Multiple users ko support
Scalability improve karna

⚙️ Setup (Kaise hota hai)
Large data centers me thousands of servers
Virtualization technology (Hypervisor) use hota hai
Physical resources ko virtual machines me divide kiya jata hai
Har user ko logically isolated environment milta hai

🔥 Use (Real Use Case)
Ek hi physical server par multiple users ke VMs run karte hain
Har user ko lagta hai ki uska dedicated server hai

👉 Example:
Ek building me alag-alag flats (shared building, private rooms)

# ☁️ 3. Rapid Elasticity

Rapid elasticity ka matlab hai ki system automatically resources ko increase (scale up) ya decrease (scale down) kar sakta hai demand ke according.

🎯 Purpose (Kyon use hota hai)
High traffic handle karna
Cost optimize karna
Performance maintain karna
Dynamic workloads support karna

⚙️ Setup (Kaise hota hai)
Auto-scaling tools configure kiye jate hain
Rules define hote hain:
CPU usage
Network traffic
System automatically:
Instances add karta hai
Ya remove karta hai
Example in Amazon Web Services:
Auto Scaling Group
Load Balancer

🔥 Use (Real Use Case)
E-commerce website pe sale chal rahi hai
Traffic suddenly increase hota hai
Servers automatically:
 2 → 20


Cloud computing enables users to access shared resources on-demand and dynamically scale them based on workload requirements.















